# Mobile First

Design the phone layout first. Desktop is an enhancement at `lg`, not the default squeezed down.

## Layout

- Default to a **single column**. Two-column grids and the persistent sidebar only from `lg:` up.
- Existing chrome: compact header + left `Sheet` below `lg`; `aside` sidebar `hidden lg:flex lg:w-56`. Do not add a bottom tab bar unless asked.
- Glanceable facts first on small screens (who, when, money, primary action). Filters and secondary blocks after.
- `min-w-0` on flex/grid children so long names and amounts do not overflow.

```tsx
// ❌ sidebar always in the flow
<div className="flex"><aside className="w-56">...</aside><main>...</main></div>

// ✅ sheet on phone, aside from lg (as in AppLayout)
<header className="lg:hidden">...</header>
<aside className="hidden lg:flex lg:w-56">...</aside>
```

## Controls

- Primary actions **full width** on mobile (`w-full`), `sm:w-auto` after that.
- Tap targets at least `min-h-11`. Do not ship `h-9` chips as the only way to switch views on a phone.
- Dialogs already used as modals; keep them usable on a narrow screen (scroll, full-width actions). Do not nest a second back control next to the header menu.
- Dense tables and multi-field filter rows: stack or collapse below `md`; keep the list scannable.

## Desktop-only

- Persistent sidebar, week/month calendar grid density, wide filter rows: `lg:` / `md:` as today.
